bfs installs a command-line tool, not a linkable library:

    <installed-prefix>/tools/bfs/bfs

Only native Linux and macOS are supported. This port explicitly disables optional
libacl, libcap, libselinux, liburing, and Oniguruma integrations; unavailable
features are governed by upstream bfs behavior. The portable POSIX regex backend
is not the application's PCRE2 backend.

For build-time use, declare { "name": "bfs", "host": true } in your manifest
on a supported host and locate the executable under the host installed prefix.
